{%- comment -%}
  One product's directions inside the "How to take it" card. If Enhanced Support is on for this product and its
  label has an enhanced direction, the label text is shown as two blocks (Daily Support, Enhanced Support);
  otherwise the label text is shown as is. The two blocks are just the label sentence cut at "For enhanced support,",
  so together they read exactly like the label. Static content: nothing here reads or changes the purchase options.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture dir_text -%}{%- render 'product-directions', p: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign dir_text = dir_text | strip -%}
{%- if dir_text != blank -%}
  <div class="how-to-take__item">
    {%- if show_title -%}<h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign enhanced_marker = 'For enhanced support, ' -%}
    {%- if show_enhanced and dir_text contains enhanced_marker -%}
      {%- assign dir_parts = dir_text | split: enhanced_marker -%}
      <div class="how-to-take__grid">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Daily Support</span><p>{{ dir_parts[0] | strip | escape }}</p></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Enhanced Support</span><p>{{ enhanced_marker | append: dir_parts[1] | strip | escape }}</p></div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <p>{{ dir_text | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
